    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 79.66 efficiency score, buoyed by a highly favorable matchup against Quintana. While the platoon disadvantage against a southpaw typically suppresses output, the combination of a generous 5.24 xERA for the opposing starter and a premier spot in the two-hole provides the necessary leverage for a massive day. **Josh Naylor** (72.02) and **James Wood** (69.92) round out our tier-one plays. **James Wood** specifically benefits from an ideal leadoff role and solid underlying metrics, while **Josh Naylor** capitalizes on the platoon advantage against Lugo to anchor the heart of the order.\n\nSecondary value is heavily concentrated in the top of the lineup, where **Zach McKinstry** (65.79) provides a surprising boost thanks to a +16% park factor adjustment that pushes his total well above his baseline. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Brice Turang** (49.06) and **Cole Young** (47.80); both face the significant hurdle of an \"Elite Hold\" pitcher, which directly penalizes our pursuit of scarce stolen bases. **Jose Caballero** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine (47.06). While he remains a vital speed asset, a combination of an unfavorable wind-in factor and an aggressive negative adjustment for his platoon matchup against Rasmussen kept him on the bench in favor of higher-floor options. \n\nWe are monitoring the risk associated with **Dalton Rushing** (51.29), as his placement in the #7 spot and the opponent's ability to suppress baserunners dampen his overall utility. We remain at full strength, though with **Mickey Moniak** currently sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested. Ensure that **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Carson Williams**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Henry Bolte** remain ready should any late-inning weather alerts or lineup shifts force a pivot to our bench reserves.",
